{"judge_label": "committed_silent", "justification_span": "Female, age 71, creatinine 0.76.\n\nFor females, κ = 0.7, α = -0.241.\nSince Scr 0.76 > 0.7, use max ratio.\n\nScr/κ = 0.76/0.7 = 1.0857\n\nFormula: 142 × min(Scr/κ,1)^(-0.241) × max(Scr/κ,1)^(-1.200) × 0.9938^age × 1.012\n\nmin = 1, so min^(-0.241) = 1\nmax = 1.0857, max^(-1.200):\nln(1.0857) = 0.08226\n× -1.200 = -0.09871\nexp(-0.09871) = 0.9060\n\n0.9938^71:\nln(0.9938) = -0.006219\n× 71 = -0.44157\nexp(-0.44157) = 0.6431\n\nNow: 142 × 1 × 0.9060 × 0.6431 × 1.012\n142 × 0.9060 = 128.65\n× 0.6431 = 82.74\n× 1.012 = 83.73\n\nFINAL: 84"}